    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25691" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lallo</span></b> , āvi, ātum, 1,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. n., to sing
				lalla</i> or <i>lullaby, to sing as a nurse to a
				child</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iratus mammae, lallare recusas,</span>”
				<i>will not let yourself be sung to sleep</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					3, 17</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 14, 3</span></i>: lallare
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαβάζειν</span>, Gloss.
		Philox.</div>
